00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:13,000
VibeGuard combines chat, durable memory, and measured harness improvement. This real chat recalls our project goal from Atlas, and both conversation turns have independently verified records.

2
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Relevant popups explain what is happening as you build. Here, a real memory rate limit triggered a proposed change.

3
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:37,000
A live model proposed a sixty-second recall cooldown. Across seven frozen incident replay cases, avoidable recall attempts fell from eight to zero. All fifty-one simulated conversation turns remained recorded. These are replay results.

4
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:52,000
RRFlow opens the exact policy for human review. The user chooses a decision and submits it explicitly. This proposal is still pending. Activation and a rerun tied to the approved version remain next.

5
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:58,000
The goal is a harness that improves while preserving continuity and human control.
